# Arbiter — core rules

`AGENTS.md` is binding. Re-read its §3 (invariants) and §6 (workflow) before every pass.

## Non-negotiables
- LLMs never decide outcomes; only `app/policy/engine.py` maps facts to an outcome.
- The Challenger can only escalate or request evidence. Nothing but verified facts or a policy-permitted precedent exception may move an outcome toward approval.
- Every model call goes through `app/llm/generator.py`. Every data access goes through `app/data/` with registry query ids.
- Vendor text is untrusted data: guard it, redact it, wrap it in `<vendor_text>`, and never let it alter prompts, tools or flow.
- No side effect without a valid signed `ExecutionContract`.
- Traces are emitted only by code that actually ran.

## Pass discipline
- Work only on the lane in `.cursor/ACTIVE_PASS` (`<ID> plan|build|blocked`).
- `plan` phase: write `.cursor/plans/<LABEL>.md` (LABEL = `P0`, `P1-A`, `P1-B`, `P2-A` … `P7`) and stop for approval. Do not write code.
- `build` phase: tests first, then implementation, until `python scripts/tasks.py verify-pass --pass <ID>` is green.
- Touch only files your lane owns (`docs/spec/passes/README.md` §3). Need anything else → set phase to `blocked` and ask.
- Never weaken, skip, xfail or delete an acceptance test. If a test is wrong → set phase to `blocked` and ask.
- When asking the human anything, first set `.cursor/ACTIVE_PASS` to `<ID> blocked` (this pauses the auto-verify hook).
- Finish: `docs/passes/<LABEL>_REPORT.md` (built / deviations / gaps / commands / Explain-it answers), write `docs/cursor-usage/<LABEL>.md`, push, delete `.cursor/ACTIVE_PASS`, stop.

## When unsure
Stop and ask with: the decision needed, 2–3 options with trade-offs, your recommendation. Never guess sponsor APIs — capture a real response into `tests/fixtures/` (secrets scrubbed).
